  "label": "The text 'partial arts' maps to the visual depiction of martial artists performing incomplete or half-hearted stances.",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'partial arts' is superimposed over the image of an adult and a child in martial arts uniforms and stances. The mapping is based on the visual implication that their martial arts practice is incomplete or inadequate, which contrasts with the serious discipline martial arts represents. The text puns on 'partial' (incomplete) and 'arts' (martial arts), creating an ironic mapping where the visual material (the martial artists) is interpreted as embodying the concept of 'partial arts'. This mapping is central to the meme's humor and its harmful intent of trivializing martial arts.",
